            "modalVerb": "missing",
            "action": "missing"
          },
          "originalNotes": "It is non-atomic because the request includes multiple separate behaviors: Signal should show a chart of how many contacts are on Signal, show how many sent messages are encrypted, allow the user to tap chart elements to see people in each category, and possibly display gamified progress messages.",
          "base": {
            "reqId": "6362-Signal",
            "requirementId": "6a3ac956be1bfa9e45d331c9",
            "phase": "main",
            "order": "65",
            "pragyanIncomp": "1",
            "nlDescription": "I have:   searched open and closed issues for duplicates  read https://github.com/WhisperSystems/Signal-Android/wiki/Submitting-useful-bug-reports  It'd be nice if Signal had a screen that would show e.g. a pie chart that indicated how many of my contacts were on Signal. Or how many of the messages I send are encrypted. Tapping an element of the pie chart would then show a list of people in that category - this would be a nice way to get an overview of contacts I still need to convince to convert. There's probably also room for some gamification in here - the app could display something like e.g. \"Almost there! __\" when most, but not all, of my contacts were using Signal.",
            "nlText": "Request Number - 6362 | Request Title - Visual display for how many contacts are on Signal | Request Description - I have:   searched open and closed issues for duplicates  read https://github.com/WhisperSystems/Signal-Android/wiki/Submitting-useful-bug-reports  It'd be nice if Signal had a screen that would show e.g. a pie chart that indicated how many of my contacts were on Signal. Or how many of the messages I send are encrypted. Tapping an element of the pie chart would then show a list of people in that category - this would be a nice way to get an overview of contacts I still need to convince to convert. There's probably also room for some gamification in here - the app could display something like e.g. \"Almost there! __\" when most, but not all, of my contacts were using Signal.",
